menu "Display unit"

config DASH_DEV_DEMO_BUTTON
    bool "Always-visible DEMO button (development)"
    default y
    help
        Shows a small DEMO button in the bottom-left corner on every screen that opens
        the demo scene picker without the parent PIN. Turn off for the car.

config DASH_LOG_FPS
    bool "Log rendered frames per second"
    default y
    help
        Prints the number of LVGL refreshes per second to the console.

config DASH_LVGL_CORE1
    bool "Pin the LVGL task to core 1"
    default y
    help
        The RGB panel's bounce-buffer copy runs as an ISR on core 0 (about a third of that core).
        Pinning the LVGL task to core 1 keeps rendering off it: measured 5-7 % less draw time per frame.

config DASH_PCLK_MHZ
    int "RGB panel pixel clock, MHz"
    range 16 40
    default 21
    help
        The panel refreshes at pclk / (1369 * 637) Hz: 21 MHz gives 24 Hz, 26 MHz about 30 Hz. LVGL
        is synchronised to the refresh, so this is the frame-rate ceiling (rendering takes 1-15 ms per
        frame, far less than the 41 ms of one refresh). Tested on the 5B panel: 26 MHz already flickers and shows
        artifacts (PSRAM bandwidth for the bounce buffer refill). Keep 21.

config DASH_RGB_BOUNCE
    bool "Use the RGB panel bounce buffer (keep on)"
    default y
    help
        With the bounce buffer the panel is fed from a small internal-RAM buffer that an ISR on core 0
        refills from the PSRAM frame buffers (about a third of core 0, ~14 ms per frame). Turning it off
        lets the panel DMA read PSRAM directly and frees that core time, but while the CPU renders into
        PSRAM the picture can flicker, shift sideways or tear. Tested on the 5B panel: without it the picture
        flickers and shifts sideways constantly. Keep it on.

config DASH_DEMO_THEME_CYCLE
    bool "Autodemo cycles the gauge themes (profiling aid)"
    default n
    help
        While the autodemo runs, switch to the next gauge theme every 10 s. Lets the frame profiler
        cover all four themes without touching the panel.

endmenu
